  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x2018;Rooted in Diversity: Partnerships for Food Security and Livelihoods&#x2019; initiative will empower small-scale food producers in Niger, Malawi and Uganda. It prioritizes local knowledge and skills to improve food production and consumption in marginal andvariable agroecologies, driven by the potential of agrobiodiversity to ensure food and nutrition security and climate resilience.

This effort, led by PELUM Uganda alongside Oxfam Novib and CIRAD, is dedicated to driving systemic change. It prioritizessocial cohesion, inclusion, and the rights of vulnerable populations through proven methodologies and collective action. The implementation consortium involves grassroots organizations with a strong track record, representing farmers, CSOs, and researchers, with diverse cultural backgrounds and a collective capacity to strengthen the role of farmers as pivotal contributors and decision-makers in tackling food insecurity.

The consortium of PELUM, OXFAM and CIRAD will oversee the implement the project in three countries (Uganda, Malawi and Niger) on four outcomes:
-             Outcome 1 Improving recognition of and access to crop diversity for local food and nutrition security
-             Outcome 2 Improve opportunities to increase income and livelihood through local value chains of agrobiodiverse products
-             Outcome 3 Support innovative farmer-researcher partnerships and collaborative ways of working among farmer organisations and researchers
-             Outcome 4: Promote collaborative environment for systemic food and agriculture policy change&#x201d;: partly covered but need capacity from &#x201c;policy specialist

Implementation in Niger will be led by two smallholder farmers&#x2019; associations. The Federation des Unions de Groupements Paysans du Niger (FUGPN Mooriben) has a network of approximately 58,000 small-scale food producers, of which 63% are women. The F&#xe9;d&#xe9;ration des Unions de Producteurs de Maradi Gaskiya (Fuma Gaskiya) provides agro-ecological options to smallholder farmers.

Ugandaimplementation will be carried out by PELUM Uganda, Oxfam in Uganda, and ESAFF Uganda(Eastern and Southern Africa Small-scale Farmers&#x2019; Forum) &#x2013; the largest small-scale farmer-led advocacy movement in the country, with a membership of more than 380,000 farmers.

Oxfam in Malawi will implement the project on country level with two national partners. the Circle for Integrated Community Development (CICOD) and Evangelical Lutheran Development Service (ELDS). CICOD will contributeits experience working withvulnerable and marginalized communities around livelihoods, security and natural resources and climate change management to promote local ownership. The Evangelical Lutheran Development Service (ELDS) will tap into its wide experience in facilitating farmer cooperatives via FFS, coupled with community-based vocational training for youth and micro-finance strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
